{
  "summary": "This experiment tested a single-modality RNA-only model using PCA_n2000 encoding, without image data or fusion, as a baseline comparison to the multimodal config_016. The validation accuracy of 0.4849 is lower than config_016's 0.5266, suggesting multimodal approaches may offer performance benefits. However, the lack of direct comparison to other single-modality baselines leaves uncertainty about whether the RNA encoder or fusion methods specifically drive the performance difference."
}

